<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04RJ">Remark <span data-tag="04RJ">10.1.2.10</span>.</a> Let $X_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial object of an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Corollary <a data-tag="04RF" href="/tag/04RF">10.1.2.7</a> asserts that an object $X \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a geometric realization of $X_{\bullet }$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04QT" href="/tag/04QT">10.1.1.3</a>) if and only if it is a geometric realization of the underlying semisimplicial object of $X_{\bullet }$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04RH" href="/tag/04RH">10.1.2.9</a>). In particular, $X_{\bullet }$ admits a geometric realization if and only if its underlying semisimplicial object admits a geometric realization. </p>
